NQPTP 1.2.9 creates a client's shared memory interface on its first control message. The app's root
script calls NQPTP up once the default one exists (RootScript.kt), which 1.2.8 created at start: on
Android, create it at start again.

diff --git a/nqptp.c b/nqptp.c
index 7a41cbe..fbded29 100644
--- a/nqptp.c
+++ b/nqptp.c
@@ -265,6 +265,12 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv) {
 
   char buf[BUFLEN];
 
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+  // The app's root script calls NQPTP up once this region exists (RootScript.kt), as with 1.2.8:
+  // create the default client's now, not on Shairport's first message.
+  get_client_id((char *)NQPTP_INTERFACE_NAME);
+#endif
+
   // open control socket
   open_sockets_at_port("localhost", NQPTP_CONTROL_PORT,
                        &sockets_open_stuff); // this for messages from the client
